  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical advice on Terms of Reference (ToR) development for Dutch-Colombian cooperation on the topic of coastal erosion San Andr&#xe9;s</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of the Netherlands, through the Partners for Water programme, has worked on the topic of coastal erosion with the Gobernaci&#xf3;n del Departamento Archipi&#xe9;lago de San Andr&#xe9;s, Providencia y Santa Catalina (hereafter: Gobernaci&#xf3;n) since 2019, focusing on the concept of nature-based solutions (NbS) as a strategy to combat coastal erosion.An investigative study for Spratt Bight identified several &apos;Building with Nature&apos;-related strategies that may be applicable for addressing coastal erosion on that part of the island. These activities build on the collaboration with the Ministry of Environment of the Government of Colombia on the development of the Plan Maestro de Erosi&#xf3;n Costera (PMEC).The past year, discussions about the continuation of the bilateral collaboration have focused on a different area of the island, also connected to messages conveyed by the Contralor&#xed;a and Procuradur&#xed;a of the Government of Colombia.It is the aim to continue the collaboration with the Gobernaci&#xf3;n, environmental agency CORALINA and other relevant governmental institutions, focused on project preparation activities for specific interventions related to combating coastal erosion.The assignment described in this Terms of Reference (ToR) document focuses on technical advice on the ToR development for a future project, supported by the Government of the Netherlands, through the Partners for Water programme. The geographical focus area of the future project (and thus also of this ToR) is the area between Sound Bay and San Luis, on the island of San Andr&#xe9;s.</narrative>
  </description>
